cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use OSCAR, please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  OSCAR: single-cell demultiplexing, counting and quality control for
  multimodal 10x Genomics libraries
abstract: >-
  OSCAR is a Nextflow DSL2 pipeline that takes a raw BCL folder and a
  samplesheet and returns demultiplexed FASTQs, count matrices and quality
  control output. It covers scRNA-seq, scATAC-seq, Multiome, DOGMA, ASAP-seq,
  CITE-seq, Flex (Fixed RNA Profiling), VDJ and CRISPR libraries. Demultiplexing
  uses BCL Convert with per-sample OverrideCycles, counting uses cellranger
  multi, cellranger-atac, cyto and kallisto/bustools, and quality control adds
  fastp, MultiQC, CellBender, Scrublet, AMULET, mgatk2, MACS3 and donor
  demultiplexing with cellsnp-lite and vireo.
type: software
